# Build output
bin/
obj/
[Dd]ebug/
[Rr]elease/
*.user
*.suo
*.userprefs

# IDE / editor state
.vs/
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*~

# Test and coverage artifacts
TestResults/
*.trx
*.coverage
coverage*.xml
coverage*.json

# Evaluation harness output. The harness writes its reports next to the test
# binaries, which bin/ and obj/ already exclude; these patterns are a safety net
# for reports written anywhere else. The evaluation *fixtures* under
# tests/AppTrace.Core.Tests/Evaluation/ are source and must stay tracked, which is
# why there is deliberately no `evaluation/` directory rule here.
*-report.txt

# Temporary probes and one-off scripts used during development
/tmp/
/scratch/
*.tmp

# Local scan output. A full scan of a real machine is a complete software
# inventory and can be hundreds of megabytes; it is useful locally and must never
# be published. The deterministic fixtures under tests/ are the tracked equivalent.
scan.json
scan*.json
*sample-scan*.json
evidence-probe.md
samples/

# Development handover notes. Local working document for whoever picks the project
# up next; deliberately not published.
docs/HANDOVER.md

# Logs and crash artifacts
*.log
*.dmp
*.etl
*.wer
crashdumps/

# OS noise
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
